1
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,700
If you've ever pasted an AI email,

2
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:14,450
hit send,

3
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:18,200
and felt your stomach drop —

4
00:00:18,250 --> 00:00:21,950
because it didn't sound like you —

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,700
you're not bad at AI.

6
00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:29,450
You skipped the human step.

7
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:33,200
Today: one idea, one skill, one action.

8
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:36,950
Keep the draft. Recover your voice.

9
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,687
Picture this.

10
00:00:41,737 --> 00:00:46,424
You asked AI for a "professional follow-up email.

11
00:00:46,474 --> 00:00:51,161
"

12
00:00:51,211 --> 00:00:55,897
It arrived polished, smiling, and strangely empty —

13
00:00:55,947 --> 00:01:00,634
"I hope this email finds you well"

14
00:01:00,684 --> 00:01:05,371
"leverage synergies"

15
00:01:05,421 --> 00:01:10,108
"circle back at your earliest convenience.

16
00:01:10,158 --> 00:01:14,845
"

17
00:01:14,895 --> 00:01:19,582
You sent it anyway.

18
00:01:19,632 --> 00:01:24,318
Your colleague replied: "This doesn't sound like you.

19
00:01:24,368 --> 00:01:29,055
"

20
00:01:29,105 --> 00:01:33,792
Or worse — nobody said anything, and you felt the cringe alone.

21
00:01:33,842 --> 00:01:38,529
I've seen this with marketers, teachers writing parent notes,

22
00:01:38,579 --> 00:01:43,266
admins writing client replies, graduates polishing CV bullets —

23
00:01:43,316 --> 00:01:48,003
women who are warm in person and plastic on the page

24
00:01:48,053 --> 00:01:52,739
the moment AI drafts for them.

25
00:01:52,789 --> 00:01:57,476
Here's the truth:

26
00:01:57,526 --> 00:02:02,213
AI can start the sentence.

27
00:02:02,263 --> 00:02:06,950
Only you can sound like you.

28
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:16,181
The problem isn't that AI writes.

29
00:02:16,231 --> 00:02:25,412
The problem is we treat the first draft as the final voice.

30
00:02:25,462 --> 00:02:34,642
Fluency tricks us.

31
00:02:34,692 --> 00:02:43,873
If it sounds smooth, we assume it's ready.

32
00:02:43,923 --> 00:02:53,104
Smooth is not the same as true.

33
00:02:53,154 --> 00:03:02,335
So let's separate three things:

34
00:03:02,385 --> 00:03:11,565
One — Drafting is labour AI can share.

35
00:03:11,615 --> 00:03:20,796
Two — Buzzwords are camouflage, not professionalism.

36
00:03:20,846 --> 00:03:30,027
Three — Your specific details are the trust signal.

37
00:03:30,077 --> 00:03:39,258
If your value is only "I can generate text,"

38
00:03:39,308 --> 00:03:48,488
yes, that layer is crowded.

39
00:03:48,538 --> 00:03:57,719
If your value includes judgment, relationship, and lived context —

40
00:03:57,769 --> 00:04:06,950
your edit is the product.

41
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:11,950
Here's the skill.

42
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:16,950
Framework name: THE HUMAN EDIT LOOP

43
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:21,950
Step 1 — Draft.

44
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:26,950
Let AI give you a first version.

45
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:31,950
Ask for structure, not personality.

46
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:36,950
Example: "Draft a short email confirming Thursday 10:

47
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:41,950
00, warm professional South African English, no buzzwords.

48
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:46,950
"

49
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:51,950
Step 2 — Strip.

50
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:56,950
Delete empty phrases.

51
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:01,950
Kill: leverage, synergy, delve, tapestry, "I hope this finds

52
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:06,950
you well" if you never say that.

53
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:11,950
Cut anything you wouldn't say out loud to a colleague in

54
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:16,950
Braamfontein or Polokwane.

55
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:21,950
Step 3 — Stamp.

56
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:26,950
Add one true detail only you would know:

57
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:31,950
the project name, the child's class, the exact invoice number,

58
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:36,950
the joke you share, the real reason for the delay.

59
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:41,950
Then read it aloud.

60
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:46,950
If your mouth trips, your reader will too.

61
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:51,950
That is the Human Edit Loop.

62
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:56,950
Draft. Strip. Stamp.

63
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:01,950
You stop sounding like a template —

64
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:06,950
and you start sending work that carries your name honestly.

65
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:15,521
Quick psychology — not as a diagnosis, as a tool.

66
00:06:15,571 --> 00:06:24,093
Embarrassment after a fake-sounding message is feedback.

67
00:06:24,143 --> 00:06:32,664
Your nervous system noticed a mismatch between identity and output.

68
00:06:32,714 --> 00:06:41,236
Don't spiral.

69
00:06:41,286 --> 00:06:49,807
Edit.

70
00:06:49,857 --> 00:06:58,379
Embarrassment is data.

71
00:06:58,429 --> 00:07:06,950
Data asks for a stamp of truth — not a vow to never use AI again.

72
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:12,664
Your action today — under thirty minutes:

73
00:07:12,714 --> 00:07:18,379
1. Generate one AI draft for a real email, WhatsApp, or CV line.

74
00:07:18,429 --> 00:07:24,093
2. Strip every buzzword and empty opener.

75
00:07:24,143 --> 00:07:29,807
3. Stamp one true detail, read it aloud, and save the final version.

76
00:07:29,857 --> 00:07:35,521
When you're done, you will not have quit AI.

77
00:07:35,571 --> 00:07:41,236
You will have practised FutureHer communication:

78
00:07:41,286 --> 00:07:46,950
one idea, one skill, one action.

